easytier-core: restore the implicit `smoltcp` feature dropped by `dep:` syntax

cargo-auditable (used by rustPlatform.buildRustPackage) runs
`cargo metadata --features <enabled features of the crate being built>`,
and `cargo metadata` applies that list to *every* workspace member. The
`easytier` crate enables a feature named `smoltcp`, but easytier-core
declares smoltcp as `optional = true` and only mentions it via `dep:`
in `proxy-packet`, so cargo aborts with:

    package `easytier-core v2.7.0` does not have feature `smoltcp`

Adding the target -> `dep:` alias brings the feature name back without
changing the build: easytier-core still only pulls smoltcp in through
`proxy-packet` / `proxy-smoltcp-stack`.

Not needed by plain `cargo build`, only by the auditable/provenance path.

diff --git a/easytier-core/Cargo.toml b/easytier-core/Cargo.toml
--- a/easytier-core/Cargo.toml
+++ b/easytier-core/Cargo.toml
@@ -127,6 +127,7 @@ management-rpc = ["easytier-proto/api"]
 proxy-cidr-monitor = []
 rich-config-errors = ["dep:ariadne"]
 tcp-hole-punch = []
+smoltcp = ["dep:smoltcp"]
 proxy-packet = [
     "wrapped-transport",
     "dep:smoltcp",
